---
description: Emit truthful AI Development Office telemetry for AI Development Kit workflows
alwaysApply: true
---

When executing an AI Development Kit short command and the project has `.ai-kit`:

Use the kit's `scripts/emit-office-event.ps1` when accessible.

Emit truthful events at workflow boundaries only.

Examples:
- `status` -> CEO/PM/Docs reading
- `sync state` -> PM/Docs/Architect
- `review project` -> Architect/Backend/Frontend/Database/QA/Security/DevOps as each audit area is actually inspected
- `fix next` -> selected implementation role + QA/Security validation
- `validate` -> QA/Security/DevOps as gates actually run
- `continue` -> resume roles implied by current-task

Do not emit simulated progress.
Do not modify user application source code for telemetry.


## Project-local emitter requirement (v3.3.6)

Use project-local tools first:

```powershell
.\.ai-kit\tools\emit-office-event.ps1
.\.ai-kit\tools\emit-office-command.ps1
```

Do not depend on a hard-coded central kit path such as `D:\AI-Development-Kit`.

If the local emitter is missing, report telemetry tooling drift and continue the user workflow without modifying application source code.


## Office command queue
Office requests may appear in `.ai-kit/command-requests.jsonl`.
Do not pretend queued commands ran.
Consume them only through an explicit/approved Office command runner workflow.
